Map QR code taps with the preview offset in device pixels

The tap position is in logical pixels, position_preview() returns device
pixels; subtracting the offset before scaling missed the code whenever
the scale factor is above 1 and the preview is not at the top-left.

--- a/src/main.c	2026-10-19 19:41:03.662089247 -0500
+++ b/src/main.c	2026-10-19 19:41:03.697970994 -0500
@@ -778,9 +778,11 @@
                 float offset_x, offset_y, size_x, size_y;
                 position_preview(&offset_x, &offset_y, &size_x, &size_y);
 
-                int zbar_x = (x - offset_x) * scale_factor / size_x *
+                // x/y are in logical pixels, the preview position in device
+                // pixels: scale before subtracting the offset
+                int zbar_x = (x * scale_factor - offset_x) / size_x *
                              state.preview_buffer_width;
-                int zbar_y = (y - offset_y) * scale_factor / size_y *
+                int zbar_y = (y * scale_factor - offset_y) / size_y *
                              state.preview_buffer_height;
 
                 for (uint8_t i = 0; i < zbar_result->size; ++i) {
